<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abdullah Ahmad Badawi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1939">1939</a>–2025</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Abdullah Ahmad Badawi was the fifth prime minister of Malaysia, from 2003 to 2009, succeeding <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahathir-mohamad">Mahathir Mohamad</a>. He promised to fight corruption, promoted '<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a> Hadhari', a moderate approach to Islam, and won a landslide in 2004, but the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barisan-nasional">Barisan Nasional</a> lost its two-thirds majority in the 2008 election and he handed over to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/najib-razak">Najib Razak</a> in 2009.</p></div>
